# The I2C master driver's task-side path in IRAM, not flash.
#
# Measured (docs/bringup-results.md, "Where rendering's delay comes from"):
# with LVGL rendering on core 1, the first I2C transfer of every IMU sample
# took 158 us longer at the median, and the second only 54 us longer, although
# it moves 17 bytes to the first's one. That is code gone cold, not a slower
# bus: rendering evicts the driver from the cache the two cores share, and
# the first transfer of each sample pays the misses. ESP-IDF keeps only the
# ISR in IRAM by default.
[mapping:plumb_i2c_master_iram]
archive: libesp_driver_i2c.a
entries:
    i2c_master (noflash)

[mapping:plumb_i2c_hal_iram]
archive: libhal.a
entries:
    i2c_hal (noflash)
